[0.062, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m  ⎿  \u001b[39mWrote \u001b[1m75\u001b[15G\u001b[22mlines to \u001b[1m~/projects/manifest/build/reviews/w08/round-1.prompt\u001b[22m\u001b[K\r\u001b[6C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m \u001b[10G\u001b[22mYou are the adversarial r\u001b[36Gviewer \u001b[44Gor\u001b[47GMan\u001b[51Gfest, a civilisation trade gam\u001b[82G built as a consumer\u001b[103Gof\u001b[106Gthe\u001b[110GJett\r\u001b[6C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m  \u001b[10G\u001b[22mison e\u001b[17Ggine SDK (sibling che\u001b[39Gkout `../jettison`, pinned by the SDK fetch). Ano\u001b[89Gher a\u001b[95Gent (Claude)\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m  2 \u001b[22mwrote the change below. Your job is to find what is wrong with it before it is committed: bugs,\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m  3 \u001b[22mbroken rules, claims that do not hold, and designs that will cost the project later. You are not\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m  4 \u001b[22mhere to agree. A review that finds nothing should say what you tried and why it held.\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m  5 \u001b[22m\u001b[K\r\u001b[6C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 6\u001b[10G\u001b[22mRead\u001b[15Gbefore\u001b[22Gjudging:\r\u001b[6C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 7\u001b[11G\u001b[22m\u001b[K\r\u001b[6C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 8\u001b[10G\u001b[22m- `CLAUDE.md` and `AGENTS.md` (how th\u001b[48G project works; they apply to you as much\u001b[90Gas to \u001b[97Ghe\u001b[100Gauthor).\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m  9 \u001b[22m-\u001b[12G`docs/coding-standards.md`,\u001b[40Gall\u001b[44Gof\u001b[47Git.\u001b[51GManifest's\u001b[62Gmodel\u001b[68Gmodules\u001b[76Gare\u001b[80Gdeterministic:\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B   \u001b[38;2;153;153;153m… +66\u001b[12Gl\u001b[14Gn\u001b[16Gs \u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2B \u001b[3G\u001b[38;2;153;153;153mRan \u001b[1m1\u001b[22m shell command \u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2B\u001b[38;2;78;186;101m●\u001b[39m \u001b[1mWrite\u001b[22m(~/projects/manifest/build/reviews/w08/round-1.before)\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153